  "description": "Read-only source/target parameter comparison. Rows retain raw values/defaults in source and target. Normalization is typed: booleans, byte sizes, numeric values, case-insensitive enums, and trailing spaces. Identity rows remain compared; only text output folds them. An unreadable side retains error and the readable side rows become not_compared. A null at_default means no known default, no row, or redaction."
